{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/173528-need-help-converting-changeling-the-lost-to-classic-wod","id":173528,"title":"Need help converting changeling the lost to Classic WOD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-18T19:51:15-07:00","id":173528,"title":"Need help converting changeling the lost to Classic WOD","content":"I'm running a crossover game and feel like changeling the lost would work better for my setting then changeling the dreaming. What changes to I need to convert CTL to the Classic WOD rules specifically the 20th analyses rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T20:17:55-07:00","id":173568,"title":"","content":"Uh. Basically a whole system overhaul. You'd be better off using nWoD with Translation Guides for Masquerade, Apocalypse, and Ascension, rather than going the other way; you would have to rewrite CtL from the ground up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T21:08:54-07:00","id":173642,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it'd be a pretty huge job. That said, I can a think of few things that could make it easier on you:<ul><li><b>Dark Ages: Fae -- </b>A lot of what became <b>Changeling: The Lost</b> came from <b>Fae</b>: a seasonal court structure, Changelings stolen at birth, etc. The flavour is kind of a meld of <b>Dreaming </b>and <b>Lost</b></li> <li><b>The Werewolf Translation Guide -- </b>Of all three of the published Translation Guides, the Werewolf one has the most practical guide for converting the basic system differences back and forth. But it couldn't hurt to look at the <b>Vampire </b>or <b>Mage </b>guides for inspiration as well.</li> <li>I don't know a lot about <b>Dreaming</b>, but there must be powers that can stand in for <b>Lost </b>ones. I'd find as many of those as possible.</li> <li>Dice penalties = additional difficulty (so, -2 dice would become a +2 difficulty)</li> <li>Vice and Virtue more or less map to Demeanor and Nature, respectively</li> </ul><br /> Apart from that, there's not a lot to go on. I'd start by converting the template (i.e., the character creation rules), then the powers. Clarity probably works as written.<br /> <br /> Sadly, it's probably easier to run the <i>other </i>OWoD games with NWoD rules, and just use Changeling as is.<br /> <br /> Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:55:10-07:00","id":174536,"title":"","content":"I ran a game of CtL using cWoD rules, cause I kinda prefer them to nWoD1.0 (GMC rules on the other hand I'm liking quite a bit, it's funny how much a few little twists can change), but decided to take the easy way out. Pretty much everything works as it does in nWoD so if you get a dice bonus or penalty according to it then you do and the roll again at 8 or 9 rules work just like they do on nWoD. Attribute changes are the biggest problem mostly on matters relying on Composure and Resolve which should be thought out on case by case basis. Some could be showed under a WP roll while others might work better if you decided to use Virtues as per VtM (you were doing crossover after all) so you could have Self-Control rolls instead of certain Composure checks etc.<br /> <br /> With powers I went again on case by case method but kept it simple non the less, the best way to go about it in my opinion is to change only what absolutely needs to be changed.<br /> <br /> All these conversions are best made with KISS in mind just like with any traditional crossovers. I didn't find it hard and my players had no complaints throughout the game, but you can absolutely make it hard if you want to start over thinking everything.<br /> <br /> But like mentioned by Yossarian if you haven't familiarized yourself with the Dark Ages: Fae you really should. It's an awesome game, with it's only real problem being with the Echoes and their infinite and easy stacking, but it is in cWoD rules and makes for somewhat easy crossovers, especially since other supernaturals wont be causing Echoes so the stacking of them might not become an issue if the Fae player is sneaky enough.<br /> <br /> But on the conversion matter I disagree with Yossarian on the matter of trying to find CtD powers that work similarly to CtL Contracts and just use the Contracts as they are tweaking them slightly only when necessary, mostly in cases where they use or affect stats or rules that do not exist in cWoD. I at the least found this to be easy and quick method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}